==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|enm}} {{term|coppeweb|lang=enm}}, from {{term|coppe||lang=enm|spider}}, from {{term|attercoppe|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|āttercoppe|lang=ang}}, from {{term|ātor||lang=ang|poison}} + {{term|copp||lang=ang|head}} + {{term|web|lang=ang||web}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-cobweb.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[spiderweb]], or the [[remain]]s of one, especially an [[asymmetrical]] one that is woven with an irregular pattern of threads.
# One of its [[filament]]s; [[gossamer]]
# {{figurative}} Something thin and [[unsubstantial]], or flimsy and worthless; [[rubbish]].
#* Sir Philip Sidney
#*: The dust and '''cobwebs''' of that uncivil age.
# An [[intricate]] [[plot]] to [[catch]] the [[unwary]]
#* Cowper
#*: Entangled in the '''cobwebs''' of the schools.
# {{internet}} a [[web page]] that either has not been [[update]]d for a long time, or that is rarely [[visit]]ed
# The European spotted flycatcher.<!--Webster 1913-->

